description: Reuse, consistent style, and a check before pages are done
alwaysApply: true
---

# Quality bar

- Second use of a pattern goes in `js/` or `css/`, not a copy. Chrome, cues, video frames, and the elastic thumbnail pan are shared.
- Use existing tokens (type, color, spacing, focus, cues). Do not invent a one-off palette or type stack per page.
- Pages work with keyboard, `prefers-reduced-motion`, and a narrow viewport. Do not trap scroll (`overflow: hidden` on `body`).
- Blog prose is publication-ready: complete sentences, consistent tense, no typos, short paragraphs, one idea per beat.
- After changing HTML, CSS, JS, or `data/`, run `node dev/check.mjs` and fix failures before finishing. Refactor while the change is small: one job per module, no dead markup, no page-specific fork of shared chrome.

```
# ❌ finish after a visual tweak with no check
# ✅
node dev/check.mjs
```
